                    "value": "How this adjustment works",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "13pt",
                      "color": "#4B2D83"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Adjusted value $ starts from your real, measured baseline (Interaction Hours Saved) and adds a marginal delta for the ONE skill selected above, scaled by its adjustment % (100% = no change, the default with nothing selected). This never sums adjustments across multiple skills at once: Skill-Sliced Assisted Hours reflects a skill's parent Category total, repeated for every skill that shares the same category, so summing it across several skills would double- or triple-count. The Loaded Rate, Reinvestment %, and Success/Quality % sliders on the Value Calculator page still scale the final dollar figure exactly as before. The skill detail table below lists every observed skill, mapped and unmapped alike; the Skill mapping coverage % card shows what share of all skill invocations are mapped to a category.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#1B1F27"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
